 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-164", "title": "the coverage gate marks a 9/9-PASS verdict FAILED when the evaluator elides a long token inside its criterion echo", "detail": {"fingerprint": "4896e1de3b5e533e4ca9cccc8454ca26864c0a2d1871d1090bb866911e31cfd6"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-11-11 (driver tick, auger XML goal). Judge run .gitreins/history/2026-11-11/9c1182c6/verdict.json graded gitreins task AUG-121 at commit ab10427290d8 with NINE items, every one status=PASS (six authored ACs each ran its exact proof command: 1 passed / 5 passed / 1 passed / 1 passed / 1 passed / 2 passed, no skips, boardctl present on the proof PATH; three derived items also PASS), tier1 lint+secrets+tests PASS (real bash tests/gate.sh) — and the verdict still persisted passed=false because the coverage gate reported 'Coverage FAILED — ungraded' listing all six authored criteria.\n\nMECHANISM (engine/gate.py:241 check_coverage + :180 _matches): each criterion is matched against items[].criterion by exact normalized text, then by a bidirectional prefix rule. The evaluator echoed each criterion with its long PATH literal elided to '...' ('PATH=/home/kara/auger/.venv/bin:/home/kara/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin' -> 'PATH=...'), so every item's criterion text differs mid-string, not at a boundary; measured SequenceMatcher ratios per criterion: 0.9072, 0.9472, 0.9293, 0.9007, 0.9105, 0.9255. Exact match fails, prefix match fails (the divergence is interior), so all six are 'ungraded' although their items are PASS.\n\nNOT A CRITERIA DEFECT: three sibling verdicts on the same day (dd902d09 AUG-119, 35a8093c AUG-118, a9b1feeb AUG-150) matched at ratio 1.000 with equally long commands, so this is evaluator echo variance colliding with a matcher that has no interior-insensitive comparison — a 9/9-PASS verdict reported as a failure.\n\nIMPACT: any row whose criteria carry a long literal token (absolute PATH, long node-id list) can lose a genuine PASS