eral list. The evaluator echoed that criterion as \"assert t == [...]\" (SequenceMatcher ratio 0.7954 against 1.0000 for the other five), and engine/gate.py:check_coverage accepts only exact normalized text or a boundary prefix, so an INTERIOR elision can never match. Workaround proven at the criterion-authoring layer: restate the criterion compactly with no repeated literal blob (assert the set relationship and print counts 6/3, bind the kinds<->XSD equality to a named test), then re-judge the SAME task id. The fix for this row must make an interior elision matchable (token-set or subsequence matching in addition to prefix) with a negative control so it cannot degrade to always-pass. AUG-126's first verdict stays published as instrument evidence.", "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
